      "safety_car_stops_outside_sanity_filter": 119,
      "reading": "The safety-car ratio depends on the filter: about a quarter of safety-car stops measure more than 60 s (the non-pitting reference is itself erratic under a safety car), and keeping them moves the ratio above 1. The reported fraction is the wide-filter median ratio; treat it as 'somewhat cheaper than green, not well determined', which its interval says too."
